## BATCH 2 — Java Backend Model Endpoints
*Give this to Claude Code alone. Read all existing Java backend files first.*

Context to give Claude Code:
"Read all files in Java backend/src/main/java/com/stocktracker/ before making changes.
Do not break any existing endpoints."

What to build:
1. DB Migration V5__models.sql:
       CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS models (
           id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
           name            VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
           onnx_file_path  TEXT NOT NULL,
           contract        JSONB NOT NULL,
           status          VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'EXPORTED',
           -- EXPORTED, ACTIVE, STOPPED
           deploy_mode     VARCHAR(10),
           -- paper, live, null
           symbols         TEXT[],
           created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
           updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
       );

2. Model.java JPA entity mapping to models table

3. ModelRepository.java:
       findByName(String name)
       findByStatus(String status)
       existsByName(String name)

4. ModelController.java endpoints:
       POST /api/models/upload
           Accepts multipart: onnx_file + contract JSON string
           Saves .onnx file to server filesystem: /app/models/{name}.onnx
           Saves contract to models table
           Returns: { id, name, status, created_at }

       GET /api/models
           Returns list of all models: [{ id, name, status, deploy_mode,
           symbols, created_at }]

       GET /api/models/{name}
           Returns full model with contract

       POST /api/models/{name}/deploy
           Body: { mode: "paper"|"live", symbols: ["NVDA", "AAPL"] }
           Updates model status to ACTIVE
           Updates deploy_mode and symbols
           Writes deploy config to /app/models/{name}_deploy.json
           Returns updated model

       DELETE /api/models/{name}
           Sets status to STOPPED

5. ModelService.java handling the business logic

Verification:
