## BATCH 10 — Wire Everything Together
*Build on top of Batches 4-9. cpp-engine branch.*

Context to give Claude Code:
"Read ALL existing files in Anake/cpp-engine/src/ before making changes.
Wire all components together in TradingEngine.cpp."

What to build:
TradingEngine class in src/engine/TradingEngine.hpp and .cpp:

    class TradingEngine {
    public:
        TradingEngine(const EngineConfig& config);
        
        void start();
        void stop();
        
    private:
        EngineConfig config;
        ONNXModel model;
        FeatureCalculator calculator;
        MarketDataFeed feed;
        OrderExecutor executor;
        TradeLogger logger;
        
        // Current positions per symbol
        map<string, Position> positions;
        
        // Called on every new bar for every subscribed symbol
        void onBar(const string& symbol, const Bar& bar);
        
        // Decision logic
        void processSignal(const string& symbol,
                          const string& signal,
                          float confidence,
                          const Bar& bar);
        
        // Position management
        void enterLong(const string& symbol, const Bar& bar);
        void exitPosition(const string& symbol, const Bar& bar,
                         const string& reason);
        
        // Check stop loss and take profit
        void checkExitConditions(const string& symbol, const Bar& bar);
    };

The onBar flow:
    1. calculator.update(bar)
    2. if (!calculator.isReady()) return
    3. features = calculator.calculate()
    4. signal = model.getSignal(features)
    5. confidence = model.getConfidence(features)
    6. logger.logSignal(strategy_name, symbol, signal, confidence, bar.time)
    7. checkExitConditions(symbol, bar)
    8. processSignal(symbol, signal, confidence, bar)

Verification — full end to end test:
    EngineConfig config = EngineConfig::fromFile("config/rf_v1_deploy.json");
    TradingEngine engine(config);
    engine.start();
    
    // During market hours should see:
    // "New bar: NVDA close=125.40"
    // "Signal: BUY confidence=0.72"
    // "Entering long: NVDA at 125.40"
    // "Order submitted: buy 1 NVDA market"
    // Trade logged to TimescaleDB

