## BATCH 11 — HTTP Server for Java Communication
*Build on top of Batch 10. cpp-engine branch.*

Context to give Claude Code:
"Read ALL existing files in Anake/cpp-engine/src/ before making changes."

What to build:
Small HTTP server so Java backend can communicate with the engine:

    POST /engine/start
        Body: { config_path: "models/rf_v1_deploy.json" }
        Starts the engine with the given config
        Returns: { status: "started", strategy: "rf_v1" }

    POST /engine/stop
        Stops the engine gracefully
        Returns: { status: "stopped" }

    GET /engine/status
        Returns: {
            status: "running",
            strategy: "rf_v1",
            symbols: ["NVDA"],
            mode: "paper",
            trades_today: 12,
            pnl_today: 84.50
        }

    POST /engine/backtest
        Body: { symbol, bars[], contract }
        Runs bar-by-bar simulation using ONNX model
        Returns: { trades[], stats }
        This replaces the Java backtest engine for ONNX models

Use cpp-httplib for the HTTP server.
Run on port 9090.

